The data model uses a standard Star Schema:

Fact Table: 

Fact_Visits (Contains transactional records for patient encounters, billing, stay duration, service types, and satisfaction scores).

Dimension Tables:

Dim_cities ( Cities, Cities ID ) 

Dim_departments (Departments, Department IDs) 

Dim_procedures ( Procedures, Procedure IDs)

Dim_Patients (Demographics, patient IDs)

Dim_Providers (Doctor names, specialty, headshot image URIs)

Dim_Insurance (Payer names, policy details)

Dim_Date (Calendar reference table for time-intelligence calculations)
## DAX For Creating the Date Table 
##
Dim_Date = 
VAR MinDate = MIN('Fact-visits'[Date of Visit])
VAR MaxDate = MAX('Fact-visits'[Date of Visit])
RETURN
ADDCOLUMNS (
    CALENDAR(MinDate, MaxDate),
    "Year", YEAR([Date]),
    "Month No", MONTH([Date]),
    "Month", FORMAT([Date], "MMM"),
    "Year-Month", FORMAT([Date], "MMM YYYY"),
    "YearMonthSort", YEAR([Date]) * 100 + MONTH([Date]),
    "Quarter", "Q" & FORMAT([Date], "Q")
)

